# Highlighted code

C++ with a keyword, a string, a comment and a number, and a `<`, a `>` and an `&` to escape:

```cpp
#include <vector>

// Count the items that are small.
auto small(std::vector<int> const& items) -> int {
	int count = 0;
	for (auto const item : items) {
		if (item < 10 && item > 0) {
			++count;
		}
	}
	return count;
}

auto name = "a & b";
```

An alias gives the same spans, and the class is still the word that was written:

```c++
int x = 1;
```
